{"skill":{"slug":"copywriting","displayName":"Copywriting"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770341837629,"changelog":"Initial release of the Copywriting skill — write high-converting marketing copy using proven frameworks.\n\n- Provides step-by-step guidance for landing pages, headlines, CTAs, product descriptions, ads, email sequences, and more.\n- Covers core copywriting formulas: AIDA, PAS, and FAB, with clear examples.\n- Includes techniques for emotional triggers, objection handling, and trust-building with proof.\n- Offers actionable headline formulas and CTA best practices.\n- Designed for solopreneurs, marketers, and founders looking to drive action with persuasive writing.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10004,"sha256":"4d89ce0eaad0184fff057659260ebd2c25a41ff2d03a6cd598405c83ccba9ac7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1790,"sha256":"5350c868488ce417af6a25df6dd8902feafab4ea6fd4d505eab1164c5bd0d50d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036115618,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"637af1b053735bfd795f450e81bdab0a2a134daf9b3a85544b586858dc487649","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/637af1b053735bfd795f450e81bdab0a2a134daf9b3a85544b586858dc487649","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: copywriting\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. The `_meta.json` file contains standard metadata. The `SKILL.md` file provides comprehensive instructions and frameworks for an AI agent to perform copywriting tasks. It contains no executable code, external network calls, attempts at prompt injection to subvert the agent's behavior, or any other indicators of malicious or suspicious activity. All 'code' blocks are examples of marketing copy, not commands to be executed.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161752675},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789036115618},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a Markdown-only copywriting guide with no executable code, persistence, credential access, or hidden system behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request file, network, credential, browser, shell, or external API access, so its environment impact is proportionate to a writing-advice skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single non-executable SKILL.md file; metadata is empty and no scripts, dependencies, remote payloads, or install-time actions were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The routing description includes broad triggers such as \"headline\" and \"write copy\", which could activate for some general writing tasks, but the instructions themselves remain copywriting-focused and do not try to override agent safety or session goals.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, memory writes, background workers, privilege escalation, tool wrapping, or cross-session behavior is present in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill teaches marketing copywriting frameworks, headlines, CTAs, emotional triggers, objection handling, proof, and A/B testing; this is coherent with its stated purpose, though users should keep claims truthful and avoid manipulative or false scarcity.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"This skill is reasonable to install for marketing copywriting help. Review generated copy for factual accuracy, truthful claims, appropriate urgency, and whether the skill activated in a non-marketing writing context because some triggers are broad.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger concern is partly supported because the description includes generic terms like \"headline\"; this is a routing-quality issue, not a security concern, because the skill is limited to copywriting guidance and has no high-impact authority.\n[EA2] expected: The cited phrase \"don't ask before you've sold them\" refers to where to place a call-to-action in marketing copy, not to autonomous agent actions, destructive operations, financial transactions, or bypassing user confirmation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036115618}}}}}